// `std.console`: the standard streams, written through the console's root
// capability, which `std.authority`'s `console` opens from the authority
// `main` is handed. A program reaches the streams through a capability it
// was given, never through the ambient `Console` interface, so what it may
// print is what crossed from `main`. The host at a program's entry serves
// each line on standard output; standard error and standard input join it
// as the host interface grows to offer them.

/// One line, written to standard output through `console`.
pub def print(console : Cap { print }, line : String) -> [Console] Unit {
  console.print(line)
}
